WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.280
"The Best Source of Vitamin B12:
Supplements, Shots, or Fortified Foods?"

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.920
To treat vitamin B12 deficiency,

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.760
intramuscular injections,

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.160
oral pills,
or sublingual lozenges

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.080
can similarly
effectively increase

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.720
the level of vitamin B12
at sufficient doses,

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.640
but this is based
on blood level targets

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.480
rather than
assessing clinical outcomes,

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.320
in terms of symptom improvement.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.320
So, some believe
that at least initially,

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.960
injected B12 should be
the first-choice treatment

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.240
for patients
with severe B12 deficiency,

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.080
though even
with the best treatment,

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.320
neurological symptoms
may take several months

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.360
or even years to resolve,
and may never get better.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.800
So, it’s better to prevent
deficiency in the first place.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.960
B12 isn’t made
by plants or animals,

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.240
but rather by bacteria,

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.560
so, feces are
a good source of vitamin B12.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.800
That’s one of the ways
our fellow great apes,

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.640
like gorillas, get B12.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.760
Evidently dining on dung
was seen to be more common

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.800
after wet weather, though,
leading to the suggestion

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.600
that besides
its nutritional importance,

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.200
it may be just that they want
something warm to nibble on

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.840
at the end of a long, cold rain.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.240
Thankfully, since the advent
of modern sanitation,

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.760
bacteria and feces are, happily,

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.000
no longer reliable sources
of vitamin B12 for humans.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.880
A large proportion
of the bacteria in our gut

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.960
do make B12, though,

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.960
but it’s always
been thought to be produced

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.640
too far down to be absorbed.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:27.760
How do we know?

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:30.400
Because if you squirt
radioactively-labeled B12

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.600
into people’s rectums,

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.920
they don’t really seem
to absorb it.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.320
But the human colon
is about five feet long (1.5 m)

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.480
and it was just squirted in
about a foot (30 cm).

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.320
What about higher up?

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.400
No B12 uptake
from the human colon

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.160
had ever been previously
described or considered,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.080
until now.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.560
B12 was squirted
via colonoscopy

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.800
all the way up
to the beginning of the colon,

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.160
and, dun dun dun dun,

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:57.200
B12 is absorbed
in the human colon.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.520
Or at least a little bit was.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.680
Now the squirt occurred
just a few inches (5 cm)

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.120
from the end
of the small intestine,

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.960
so some of it
may have slipped out

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.240
and was absorbed there,
even higher up,

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:10.480
but presumably the same
could happen with any B12

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.640
made by our own microbiome.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:13.760
The researchers suggest

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.760
that this potential
colonic absorption

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:18.240
might help explain
an apparent paradox.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.760
There are hundreds of millions
of vegetarians in India,

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:25.200
so why don’t we see
more B12 deficiency?

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.880
Well, vitamin B12 deficiency
is endemic in India

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:33.600
with B12 deficiency rates
running as high as 50 to 77%,

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.720
but maybe the reason
it’s not closer to 100%

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:40.960
is because they’re absorbing
a bit from their microbiome.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.400
Obviously, though, it’s not
something we can count on.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.560
The safest way
to prevent B12 deficiency

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.520
in plant-based diets

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.320
is to take
an oral B12 supplement.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.160
B12-fortified foods
like certain brands

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:55.200
of nutritional yeast or soymilk
are another option,

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.680
but may only provide
adequate vitamin B12

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.320
when consumed
multiple times a day.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.280
What about chlorella
and spirulina,

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.000
which both claim
to contain B12?

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.520
But actually, up to 90%
of the so-called B12

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.600
is pseudo-B12,
B12 analogs that look like B12

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.400
but are actually unusable
by our body.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.560
It’s outrageous
that manufacturers

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.920
would advertise real B12
when there may be none.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.720
It’s crucial consumers are not
misled by wrong information.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.080
What about duckweed,
which also claims to have B12?

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:31.280
Sometimes it does,

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.840
but not because it
or any plant makes it,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.280
but because of variable amounts
of bacterial contamination.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.440
If you actually disinfect
the plants

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.520
to reduce the bacteria loads
in duckweed,

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.840
you end up with little B12.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.080
Same with seaweed like nori.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:49.440
Sometimes it’s contaminated
with B12-producing microbes,

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:50.240
other times not,

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:53.360
and sometimes it has
pseudo-B12 producing bugs.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:54.480
For example, in this study,

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.920
eating nori actually made
B12 status worse,

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.040
whereas, in this study,

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.840
nori made B12 status
mostly better,

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.160
but even then,
it made B12 status worse

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.480
in two of the participants.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:09.120
That’s why those eating
unfortified plant-based diets

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.280
must take B12 supplements.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.040
But which kind is best?

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.800
If you ask ChatGPT,

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.600
it says methylcobalamin
and adenosylcobalamin

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.440
are better than cyanocobalamin,

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.160
but ChatGPT is wrong.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:23.360
(It must have just sucked up

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.480
all that slimy supplement
company propaganda.)

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:29.920
Check out my video
on why cyanocobalamin is best

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.083
for most people.

